Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:51:59 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(sync): extract head-to-head, form, and per-match
 news from ESPN summary
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ESPN's summary payload carries three blocks we were throwing away:
`seasonseries[0]` (last 5 meetings between the two teams),
`lastFiveGames[0..1]` (both teams' last 5 results), and a `news`
block (articles tagged to BOTH teams in this match).

Three new tables store them, refreshed on every summary sync:
match_head_to_head, match_form, match_news. Three new normalizers
in normalize.ts shape the JSON. applySummary upserts all three inside
its existing transaction.

No new ESPN calls — these were always in the payload, just unused.
The next commit wires them to MatchDetail tabs.

