Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TabBar: forwardRef<HTMLElement, {}> tripped no-empty-object-type.
Dropping the empty props generic (forwardRef<HTMLElement>) is the
fix that compiles here — Record<string, never> rejects the ref
AppShell passes through to the bar, because the index signature
makes `ref` incompatible.

useApi: `favoritesQuery.data?.teams ?? []` minted a fresh array
every render, so the `ids` memo and isFavorite changed identity on
each pass. Memoize `teams` on the query data instead.

MatchDetail: `nf` (Intl.NumberFormat) was rebuilt every render
inside the countdown memo's dependency closure. Memoize it per
locale and depend on it.

The match-card polish this commit was to carry (full-width league
meta, white kickoff time on upcoming cards) is already the state of
the shipped card: the feed's MatchRow in LeagueGroup.tsx renders
the kickoff clock in text-ink, and the league label lives in the
group header with no count-chip width reservation to fight.

